³1ip³262.225.252.246³2ts³21074836280³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3<b>[[Non-Aggression Principle]] Talk</b>

040122, JunkerIn

asking now myself-- What is ZAP?
my idea might be 'wrong'.
at 0ip.com i find: nothing
adjudicator to compel attending a 'court' procedure.
after the 'hot' situation of self-defense, it all seems hear-say, and thus no excuse for initiating violence, adjudicator or not.
BillStClair resp of 040121 read & saved on my disk, thanks, it's a start.
<b>i'll still be hunting the trail...</b>
Google hits: ZAP-279 & NAP-973, not much, sorta odd. Is ZAP-NAP-ancap actually very limited? Are all those sites I thought I was at really political libertarians going for the golden ring of power? Am I naive?
Have yet to read anyone talking about the base or the implications (except anti-abortion or gen defunct of state).
More reading to do.

040123, JunkerIn: pre-aggression - aggression/defense - post-aggression
